**Fix readConfig(json)**

`readConfig(json)` hides broken input by returning `{}`, so callers never find out the config is invalid. Let a parse error reach the caller, but keep returning `{}` for empty or blank text.

```js
function readConfig(json) {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(json);
  } catch {
    return {};
  }
}
```

back:
// Why: Swallowing an error turns "your file is broken" into "you have no settings". Handle
// the case you expect (empty text) and let real errors propagate.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/parse
function readConfig(json) {
  if (json.trim() === "") return {};
  return JSON.parse(json);
}

